{'name': "Elsie's", 'address': '117 W De La Guerra St', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Bars, Nightlife, Coffee & Tea, Food, Internet Cafes', 'hours': {'Monday': '7:30-2:0', 'Tuesday': '7:30-2:0', 'Wednesday': '7:30-2:0', 'Thursday': '7:30-2:0', 'Friday': '7:30-2:0', 'Saturday': '16:0-2:0', 'Sunday': '16:0-2:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': True, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'free', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': False, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': True, 'Ambience': {'romantic': False, 'intimate': False, 'touristy': False, 'hipster': True, 'divey': False, 'classy': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'casual': False}}, 'business_stars': 4.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2021-08-16 20:56:48', 'review_text': "I've been coming to this place since I moved to SB; such a friendly and warm environment, Love meeting new people there, the service is great and staff are lovely!"}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2021-07-08 22:33:32', 'review_text': 'Bottom Line:  A great little bar\n\n\n\nI CANNOT believe that I have never been to this place especially since I grew up in this town.\n\nI love everything about this place; engine block coffee table, Cagiva gas tank in the rafters, lost of comfy places to sit, patio in the front and the back....the bar tender was super friendly and the people there were cool... and its got Pac Man!\n\nLoved the Boont Amber too.  Check out this spot if you havent'}, {'review_stars': 3.0, 'review_date': '2021-04-15 12:22:25', 'review_text': "Nice little hole-in-the-wall spot. \n\nIf you're searching for Elsie's, you'll likely drive right past it. It's not really advertised from the street and I believe that this is intentional. While only a mere block or so from the best of downtown, its location is far enough off the beaten path that lends to the feeling of a speakeasy.\n\nElsie's is in a unique old building sectioned off into a few rooms. You'll find old couches (the kind you'll absolutely sink into), vibrant wall colors, and eclectic wall art. It's like a grunge-style garage from the '90s and truly brings me back to that era. There's also a great, large back patio along with a small front parklet area for Covid. There are two bathrooms which have seen far better days, but their dirtiness ties right into the old, endearing vibe of the place as a whole. \n\nElsie's is beer and wine only - and cash only, although there's an ATM in front. I don't typically carry cash so must remember this fact when I come here. You'll find a very unique assortment of beers and I've tried a few good ones. I'd also tried their soju-based Bloody Mary once and it wasn't bad. \n\nWhy three stars? Service can be a hit or a miss. I was here last night and the bartender was awesome. He was able to recommend some good beers for us and even provided a shot glass with a sample to try. Haven't always been this lucky, though. I was here about a year and a half ago (late 2019) and the female bartender working (dark hair, she's there often) was surly to the point that I'd decided not to come back in until just yesterday. I don't know if she's still here but I'd avoid at all costs if she is. Otherwise, a nice, comfortable local watering hole."}]}
